post_install() {
    cat <<'MSG'
graphs1090 collects through collectd and reads dump1090's stats from /run/dump1090. To finish:
  1. cp /usr/share/graphs1090/collectd.conf /etc/collectd.conf
  2. lighttpd: add to /etc/lighttpd/lighttpd.conf
       server.modules += ("mod_alias", "mod_redirect", "mod_setenv")
       include "conf.d/graphs1090.conf"
     nginx: include /usr/share/doc/graphs1090/nginx-graphs1090.conf in your server {} block.
  3. systemctl enable --now collectd graphs1090
Optional: /usr/share/graphs1090/malarky.sh keeps the RRD files in RAM and flushes them when collectd
stops, sparing the SD card; it schedules a nightly collectd restart through cron.d, which needs cronie.
Graphs: http://<host>/graphs1090/  (first data after about 10 minutes)
MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
    systemctl try-restart graphs1090.service 2>/dev/null || true
}
